  "source_review": {
    "cache_c_sha256": "51379b75a3dcc80b629a3d92a5710b43b2a6c04fd13f4d7f56d01f5e7836255c",
    "facts": [
      "cache_reload creates one temporary rhash across config records, hosts files and initial hostsdir files.",
      "Duplicate name lookup rewrites matching entries next links before add_hosts_entry scans those same links for reverse ownership.",
      "Incremental hostsdir uses cache_find_by_addr with no temporary rhash, after removing the changed source UID.",
      "cache_find_by_addr enumerates every matching F_REVERSE entry; rfc1035 emits each as a PTR answer.",
      "Precise PTR order follows the C global name hash table and its growth/order, not first insertion order alone."
    ],
    "tradeoff": "Retaining F10 leaves a measured conditional missing PTR alias plus forward ordering difference; forward A membership and service health remain correct in this fixture. Full emulation needs explicit bulk state and multiple reverse answers, with further PTR ordering/lifecycle and memory validation. A first-owner map plus adjusted flags alone cannot close it."
  },
